<Panels>
  <config><![CDATA[{
  "game_id": 73,
  "created_at": "2026-05-27T23:16:38.000Z",
  "level_num": "custom",
  "user_id": 1,
  "properties": {
    "panels": [
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-combine-transformations-739e3414-ca1e-4444-862a-47041607ea8e",
        "text": "So far, we've focused on changing one object at a time. But the real power of 3D comes from arranging **multiple objects** to create a scene!",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/60f9668b241906c828ac4aebfe0ccad9-test-lesson-combine-transformations-panel-1-5f9c08b8-0652-4d76-bc29-3430bb3214d4.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-combine-transformations-c31c1adf-a12e-414e-9abb-9be6c40d55ef",
        "text": "Every object in your scene can have its own unique `position`, `scale`, and `rotation` values. This lets you place each one exactly where you want it.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/bb264d9f8b5804ea0fadec28d90422b8-test-lesson-combine-transformations-panel-2-56c2ae5f-31df-4be0-889d-f2b486b7b853.png",
        "layout": "text-top-left"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-combine-transformations-8977c29c-da81-463e-9eca-22c93a34bf54",
        "text": "These properties work together. An object's position determines its overall location, its scale defines its size and proportion, and its rotation sets its orientation in space.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/d54c7ac3d7842feb497e5fb054991d9d-test-lesson-combine-transformations-panel-3-fa81dec4-15e2-44f1-954d-f937201c8692.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-right"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-combine-transformations-01f26d9c-6a05-4dba-8fbb-462d20745cb6",
        "text": "By carefully adjusting these three properties for each object, you can build impressive static compositions, like a stack of blocks or a futuristic city.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/5863a1f3be1f1e4957b3f16997280615-test-lesson-combine-transformations-panel-4-3522bbc9-4ef4-4521-945a-430272def524.png",
        "layout": "text-top-center"
      },
      {
        "key": "test-lesson-combine-transformations-11827068-cdbd-4c24-9e2e-60bb5bde606a",
        "text": "Think of yourself as a digital architect or sculptor! You're using code to precisely define the world your users will experience.",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/eedf5d759c33eae31f08b9ffe0e458b2-test-lesson-combine-transformations-panel-5-c0909c37-cc3b-42af-a7a4-ffedb89e3e44.png",
        "layout": "text-bottom-left"
      }
    ],
    "generate_outline": "Discuss how to apply position, scale, and rotation to multiple objects independently to arrange them in a static composition. Emphasize how these properties work together to define an object's final appearance and placement."
  },
  "published": true,
  "audit_log": "[{\"changed_at\":\"2026-05-27 23:17:20 +0000\",\"changed\":[],\"changed_by_id\":1,\"changed_by_email\":\"brendan+levelbuilder@code.org\"},{\"changed_at\":\"2026-05-27 23:17:21 +0000\",\"changed\":[],\"changed_by_id\":1,\"changed_by_email\":\"brendan+levelbuilder@code.org\"}]"
}]]></config>
</Panels>
